'''a battuta''' (ä bät-tö′tä). [It.: see ''bate''<sup>1</sup>, ''batter''<sup>1</sup>.] With the beat. {{smaller|In ''music'', a direction to resume strict time after the free declamation of a singer: chiefly used in recitatives. It is equivalent to ''a tempo''. ''Grove''.}}

'''abature''' (ab′a-tūr), ''n.'' [< OF. ''abatture'', a throwing down, pl. ''abattures'', underbrush trampled down, < ''abatre'', beat down: see ''abate'', ''v.''] The mark or track of a beast of the chase on the grass; foiling.

